On Monday, September 1, 2014 10:56:25 AM UTC-4, la gleki wrote:
>
> Semantical categorization of the universe can't be done since most 
> concepts have more than one useful tag.
> Look at this attempt:
> http://mw.lojban.org/index.php?title=semantic_categorization_of_gismu
> It is not perfect and no attempt can be perfect.
>

I've no illusions about achieving perfection. In fact, I think that's a 
common fallacy about the taxonomic approach --even Wikipedia fails here by 
equating it to "philosophical language". To me its just about utilizing 
patterns to make a language easier to learn, understand and use.

(@clifford well said)

